From: Longwei Yang <19267252+Longwei-Yang@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:37:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Safarium: native extension side panels (left/right dock)

Extension side panels (e.g. Claude) were dropped in the native UI. Now
SafariumRootView docks the side panel entry's own view left (Safarium
default) or right of the page, with a native AppKit header (icon, name,
move to other side, close) and a resizable edge. The side panel UI lends
its current view to the window and reclaims it before caching/dropping
it; the detached-focus-manager property is cleared while the view is in
the widget. GetContainingWebContents no longer CHECKs on non-WebUI side
panels. Settings > Appearance shows "Side panel position" again.

Local checkpoint only; not intended for upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
